{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-report.py","line":1913,"code_snippet":"components = [a[\"id\"] for a in arms if a[\"id\"] not in (CONTROL, BARE) and not a.get(\"absent\") and a.get(\"eval_only\") is not True]","reasoning_trace":"Traced the three review-catch-only arms added at :1913 into Analysis.primaries() (:653-658): any arm with REVIEW in task_types gets [PASS, CATCH]. compare() (:731-733) restricts PASS to BUILD_TYPES; the arm has no cell on any build task, so n == 0, usable() (:577-579) is false, decide() sets nopair (:849-850) and returns the inconclusive clause (:873-877); decidable (:922) is always false.","finding":"a0_bare_fable, a1_review_only and a1_no_dissent are components whose decision can never leave {investigate, keep, inconclusive}; remove/simplify are unreachable.","critique":"The suite rules primaries_by_arm (ablation-2.0.yaml:113) know only build_only and all_types; the code maps 'contains review-catch' to all_types. No test drives a review-catch-only component to a decision.","remediation":"Add review_only: [defect_catch_rate] to rules.primaries_by_arm; return it from primaries() when task_types contains review-catch and neither all nor a build type; render 'n/a (review-only)' at :1634, :1649, :1699; add a gen-fixtures scenario reaching remove and keep for a1_review_only and assert .decidable == true.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1164.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":258,"code_snippet":"EVAL_ONLY=false; [[ \"$(jq -r '.eval_only // false' <<<\"$ARM_DEF\")\" == true ]] && EVAL_ONLY=true","reasoning_trace":"The hazard the refusal exists for is the open mount (toggles.oracle_open: true exposes review-catch answer paths). The refusal reads the declared eval_only flag; the oracle_open ⇒ eval_only coupling lives only in validate-suite.sh (:179), which pipeline-run.sh never invokes. A --suite-file with oracle_open: true and no eval_only runs the open mount with no refusal (dry run prints overlay=none(oracle_open)).","finding":"The eval_only refusal gates the declaration, not the toggle that opens the oracle; a suite file that omits eval_only runs the open mount outside any batch context.","critique":"Defense in depth: the runtime guard should key on the condition it protects against, or validate the coupling itself.","remediation":"Set EVAL_ONLY=true when either .eval_only == true or .toggles.oracle_open == true (or die when oracle_open is true and eval_only is not), so the runtime enforces what validate-suite.sh declares.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html","https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design/"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"modularity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":341,"reasoning_trace":"The dry-run config_edits list is an inline jq re-implementation of apply_arm_toggles' toggle→.loa.config.yaml mapping (lib/sandbox-mount.sh, not in the diff). Three dry-run tests (pipeline-run.bats:1195-1221) pin the copy.","finding":"Duplicated security-relevant mapping: when the library changes, the dry run misreports which gates the sandbox disables.","remediation":"Expose a plan function from lib/sandbox-mount.sh that both apply_arm_toggles and the dry run call.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1041.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-report.py","line":1913,"reasoning_trace":"a0_bare_fable has toggles.loa_mount: false and phases [BARE]; a0_bare is excluded from components by id but a0_bare_fable is not. k rises to 9 in the EFP line; the arm receives a keep/remove/simplify verdict a baseline cannot carry.","finding":"A bare baseline variant is counted as a decision component.","remediation":"Exclude loa_mount: false arms (or a declared decision_arm: false) from components; report A0F beside A0 in H1.","confidence":"medium","references":[]}
